# Configuration File Validation Rules

## Package.json Validation

- Validate that package.json contains required fields from template.json
- Ensure version follows semantic versioning standards
- Check that dependencies match those listed in package-lock.json
- Verify that scripts are consistent with those defined in build-config.json
- Ensure activationEvents match commands defined in commands-registry.json

## TypeScript Configuration

- Validate tsconfig.json settings against recommended-config.json
- Check that compiler options match project standards in tsconfig-base.json
- Ensure paths configuration is consistent with directory structure in project-layout.json
- Verify that exclude patterns match those in .gitignore

## Extension Configuration

- Validate that all commands in package.json are implemented in src/commands/
- Check that all providers are properly registered according to providers-config.json
- Ensure activation events are properly configured based on usage-patterns.json
- Verify that contribution points match the extension manifest in extension-schema.json

## Webview Configuration

- Validate webview provider implementation against webview-schema.json
- Check that all required methods are implemented in webviewProvider.ts
- Ensure HTML content includes required elements and styles from webview-schema.json
- Verify message handlers match the defined API in api-schema.json

## Component Configuration

- Validate Lit Element components against component-schema.json
- Check that all required decorators and imports are present
- Ensure component structure follows the defined schema
- Verify event handling patterns match component-schema.json

## Build Configuration

- Validate esbuild.config.js against build-schema.json
- Check that entry points match those defined in build-schema.json
- Ensure output configuration follows build-schema.json
- Verify that externals match those listed in build-schema.json

## Project Structure

- Validate directory structure against project-layout.json
- Check that all required files and directories exist
- Ensure import paths match those defined in project-layout.json
- Verify file patterns follow the established conventions

## Code Quality Configuration

- Validate ESLint configuration against coding-standards.json
- Check that Prettier configuration matches formatting-rules.json
- Ensure test configuration follows testing-standards.json
- Verify that pre-commit hooks are configured according to git-hooks-config.json

